00:00:45,187 --> 00:00:46,437
Story of the Week.

8
00:00:46,437 --> 00:00:52,850
Claude Sonnet 5 Is Here - and It's Supposed to Be Almost as Good as Opus, for a Sixth of the Price.

9
00:00:52,850 --> 00:01:01,637
Starting July 1, 2026, Anthropic is making Claude Sonnet 5 the new default model for all Free and Pro users .

10
00:01:01,637 --> 00:01:09,162
Not a quiet background update, but a direct replacement for Claude 4.6 - for millions of users all at once.

11
00:01:09,162 --> 00:01:20,200
Anthropic calls it the most "agentic" Sonnet model yet: it builds its own plans, uses tools, and operates at a level of autonomy previously reserved for larger models .

12
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:31,237
Anthropic says Sonnet 5 shows clear improvements over Sonnet 4.6 in reasoning, tool use, coding, and knowledge work - with performance approaching Opus 4.8 .

13
00:01:31,237 --> 00:01:42,362
It also brings a native 1-million-token context window plus lower rates of unwanted behavior such as hallucination and sycophancy, backed by real-time cyber safeguards .

14
00:01:42,362 --> 00:01:57,800
The real lever is price: through August 31, 2026, Sonnet 5 costs an introductory $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, rising to $3/$15 afterward .

15
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:08,312
The model () is available immediately via API, Claude Code, and the Claude Platform - across Free, Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise alike .

16
00:02:08,312 --> 00:02:12,612
"Approaching Opus 4.8" - at significantly lower cost.

17
00:02:12,612 --> 00:02:13,637
— Anthropic

18
00:02:13,637 --> 00:02:24,975
Why it matters: For developers and teams who stuck with Sonnet 4.6 over cost concerns, this means Opus-level agentic capability just became affordable at mass-market scale.

19
00:02:24,975 --> 00:02:33,175
Anyone using Claude Code or the API for coding workflows gets a more capable default model overnight, at no extra cost.

20
00:02:33,175 --> 00:02:44,300
Critical voices: It remains open how strongly "close to Opus" holds up in independent benchmarks - Anthropic's own comparison figures naturally come from the vendor itself.

21
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:52,950
Bottom Line: Sonnet 5 pushes mid-tier agentic capability up far enough that an Opus upgrade no longer makes sense for many teams.

22
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:54,287
More Top Stories.

23
00:02:54,287 --> 00:02:59,912
Claude Science Enters Public Beta - Anthropic Takes Aim at Biology's Complexity.

24
00:02:59,912 --> 00:03:08,312
Anthropic has unveiled Claude Science, an application tailored for lab and pharma research, presented at an event in San Francisco .

25
00:03:08,312 --> 00:03:20,337
CEO Dario Amodei sees it as a technology meant to help tackle the complexity of biological systems - a domain where researchers have so far had to rely solely on their own minds .

26
00:03:20,337 --> 00:03:27,525
"It's going to be a general purpose technology that helps us to make sense of that complexity, in its full complexity, better.

27
00:03:27,525 --> 00:03:29,800
We don't know for sure if that's going to work out.

28
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:33,212
But I think we're seeing signs that we're seeing the beginnings of it."

29
00:03:33,212 --> 00:03:35,925
— Dario Amodei, CEO Anthropic

30
00:03:35,925 --> 00:03:39,612
Anthropic has not yet disclosed concrete metrics or pricing .

31
00:03:39,612 --> 00:03:53,700
Still, pharma and biotech teams should take a close look: Amodei's own caution ("we don't know for sure if it's going to work out") is notably candid for a product announcement - a sign that this launches more as a research tool than a finished product.

32
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:57,762
EU Council Gives Final Green Light to Simplified AI Act.

33
00:03:57,762 --> 00:04:04,162
The Council of the European Union has given final approval to the "Simplification Package" for the AI Act .

34
00:04:04,162 --> 00:04:13,212
The key change: obligations for high-risk AI systems are pushed back to December 2027 and August 2028, respectively .

35
00:04:13,212 --> 00:04:22,012
Small and medium-sized enterprises with up to 750 employees and up to €150 million in revenue get additional relief .

36
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:32,012
At the same time, the EU is tightening rules elsewhere: a new ban targets non-consensual sexualized AI content and AI-generated CSAM material .

37
00:04:32,114 --> 00:04:45,851
For European AI teams, this means more time to prepare for compliance obligations, but no all-clear on misuse scenarios - the deadline extension applies only to high-risk systems, not the new prohibited-use provisions.

38
00:04:45,851 --> 00:04:51,326
Fable 5 Returns - and the Jailbreak Debate Exposes an Industry-Wide Problem.

39
00:04:51,326 --> 00:05:07,826
After just 18 days, Anthropic is making Claude Fable 5 globally available again starting July 1, 2026, after US export controls (imposed June 12, 2026) were lifted on June 30, 2026 .

40
00:05:07,826 --> 00:05:15,751
The export halt was triggered by a method Amazon researchers found to bypass Fable 5's safeguards and generate exploit code .

41
00:05:15,751 --> 00:05:27,589
Notably, tests showed that even weaker models such as Claude Opus 4.8, GPT-5.5, and Kimi K2.7 could identify the same vulnerabilities .

42
00:05:27,589 --> 00:05:40,464
"Many less capable models - including Claude Opus 4.8, GPT-5.5, and Kimi K2.7 - were able to identify the same vulnerabilities as Fable 5."

43
00:05:40,464 --> 00:05:41,489
— Anthropic

44
00:05:41,489 --> 00:05:55,776
Anthropic, together with Amazon, Microsoft, and Google, has proposed an industry-wide framework for rating jailbreak severity, based on four criteria: capability uplift, breadth, actionability, and discoverability .

45
00:05:55,776 --> 00:06:04,526
The new safety classifier blocks the reported bypass technique over 99% of the time, and the research team was doubled before launch .

46
00:06:04,526 --> 00:06:05,351
So what?

47
00:06:05,351 --> 00:06:16,539
The incident shows that when even weaker models find the same flaw, a security issue is rarely model-specific - industry coordination becomes a necessity, not a nice-to-have.

